{
  "facts": [
    {
      "topic": "scope",
      "statement": "The entry parses Markdown from a byte buffer, a memory-backed FILE, or a streaming parser, or converts Markdown directly to HTML. When parsing returns a document, it renders that tree as CommonMark, HTML, LaTeX, man, and XML.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c",
          "start_line": 29,
          "end_line": 71,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "These are the entry point's operation selection, calls, and render sequence."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-28b1338609409c49238f",
          "start_line": 511,
          "end_line": 569,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "configuration",
      "statement": "The supplied recipe configures with `cmake ../`, builds `cmark_static`, compiles `fuzz/cmark-fuzz.c`, and links `build/src/libcmark.a` into `cmark_fuzzer`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-944c463f7c78bc0977c2",
          "start_line": 18,
          "end_line": 25,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The build recipe fixes the target's requested build and link steps."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "trigger",
      "statement": "Inputs shorter than the packed two-int configuration are skipped. For other inputs, the first bytes supply options, mode, and width; the remainder is Markdown. The mode comes from the top two option bits, while the option mask admits SOURCEPOS, HARDBREAKS, UNSAFE, NOBREAKS, NORMALIZE, VALIDATE_UTF8, and SMART.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c",
          "start_line": 10,
          "end_line": 32,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The entry point defines the finite fuzz-input format and selection gates."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-28b1338609409c49238f",
          "start_line": 575,
          "end_line": 624,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "contract",
      "statement": "The parser contract supports creating a parser with an existing AST root. Parsing appends children after any existing children, and the stated use is creating one document from multiple parsed fragments.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-28b1338609409c49238f",
          "start_line": 483,
          "end_line": 504,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-9c7a1f87a173b7b5f605",
          "start_line": 483,
          "end_line": 504,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "counterevidence",
      "statement": "The complete harness creates its streaming parser with `cmark_parser_new(options)` and never supplies an existing root or constructed AST. The direct and file modes also receive only the Markdown remainder.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 75,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The complete entry point establishes its actual parser setup and call routes."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-28b1338609409c49238f",
          "start_line": 469,
          "end_line": 504,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": true,
      "audited_unit_ids": ["u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c"]
    },
    {
      "topic": "alternative",
      "statement": "`cmark_parser_new` is specified as using the default allocator through `cmark_parser_new_with_mem`. The harness's streaming route therefore has a supported default-allocator setup, while the separate into-root contract adds an existing-root parameter.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-28b1338609409c49238f",
          "start_line": 464,
          "end_line": 504,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c",
          "start_line": 43,
          "end_line": 55,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The streaming route calls the default parser constructor, feeds it, finishes it, and frees it."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "contract",
      "statement": "The declared default options are zero. Safe rendering is the default; `CMARK_OPT_SAFE` has no effect, and `CMARK_OPT_UNSAFE` enables raw HTML and unsafe links in HTML rendering.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-28b1338609409c49238f",
          "start_line": 575,
          "end_line": 603,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-cc847c393e2c1e8a858b",
          "start_line": 175,
          "end_line": 183,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The HTML renderer replaces raw HTML unless UNSAFE is set."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-cc847c393e2c1e8a858b",
          "start_line": 280,
          "end_line": 305,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The HTML renderer gates link and image URLs on UNSAFE or the dangerous-URL scanner."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "counterevidence",
      "statement": "Although the harness option mask omits `CMARK_OPT_SAFE`, that option is documented as having no effect; zero options already select safe mode. The mask does admit `CMARK_OPT_UNSAFE`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-28b1338609409c49238f",
          "start_line": 575,
          "end_line": 603,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c",
          "start_line": 19,
          "end_line": 22,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The complete option-mask expression shows SAFE omitted and UNSAFE admitted."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "alternative",
      "statement": "The XML renderer writes link and image destinations from the node URL, while HTML conditionally omits unsafe URLs. Thus XML provides a route to render the destination value, but its output is distinct from HTML's guarded `href` or `src` behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-d9771f5351f349eb48ec",
          "start_line": 177,
          "end_line": 187,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-cc847c393e2c1e8a858b",
          "start_line": 280,
          "end_line": 305,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The HTML URL gate establishes the different behavior."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c",
          "start_line": 64,
          "end_line": 69,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The harness invokes both renderers when it has a document."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "alternative",
      "statement": "The streaming path feeds at most 20 Markdown bytes per call. A finite Markdown remainder can place `\\r` at the end of one feed and `\\n` at the start of the next; the supplied API test shows this split-line-ending call sequence is supported.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c",
          "start_line": 43,
          "end_line": 55,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The loop fixes feed boundaries from the input remainder."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-9f64627da502cc3e4da7",
          "start_line": 903,
          "end_line": 912,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The test demonstrates a feed ending in CR followed by a feed beginning in LF."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-28b1338609409c49238f",
          "start_line": 511,
          "end_line": 519,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "scope",
      "statement": "The complete harness has no explicit `assert` or expected-output comparison. Its existing gates are the minimum-size check, the nonempty Markdown check for file mode, and the non-NULL document check before rendering; returned render buffers and the document are freed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 75,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The complete entry point establishes its existing checks and lifetime operations."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-28b1338609409c49238f",
          "start_line": 521,
          "end_line": 569,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": true,
      "audited_unit_ids": ["u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c"]
    }
  ],
